  "notes": "USAGE:\nPrimarily used as a する verb ({繁茂|はんも}する). A somewhat literary or formal word. In everyday speech, {生|は}い{茂|しげ}る (to grow thickly) is more common.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {草木|くさき}が{繁茂|はんも}する (vegetation grows luxuriantly)\n- {雑草|ざっそう}が{繁茂|はんも}する (weeds grow thickly)\n- {繁茂|はんも}した{森|もり} (a densely overgrown forest)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {生|は}い{茂|しげ}る: to grow thickly — more colloquial and commonly used in everyday speech",
